# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## What this is

This directory is a **Next.js static export** (`next build` with `output: 'export'`) of the
MLAI corporate marketing site, deployed at `https://mlai.dev`. It is **build output, not source**:
there is no `package.json`, `next.config.*`, TypeScript, JSX, or component source anywhere in
this tree. It is also **not a git repository**.

The source project that produces this export is, per workspace notes, the
`MLAI-CORPORATION-WWW` React/Bun repo. **Editing files here does not change the source** — any
change is overwritten the next time the site is exported. Make real changes in the source repo
and re-export; treat this directory as a deployable artifact for inspection, local preview, or
deployment only.

Build ID of this export: `rdWFNOHrsNL5x5mZViBIe` (same across all pages — confirms one
coherent build).

## Layout

- `index.html`, `404.html` — top-level pages.
- `<route>/index.html` — one folder per route (trailing-slash / clean-URL routing). Routes:
  `wdbx`, `abi`, `abbey`, `platform`, `services`, `research`, `architecture`, `company`,
  `investors`, `contact`, plus `404/`.
- `<route>/index.txt` — the **RSC flight payload** for that route (serialized React Server
  Component tree the client hydrates from). The human-readable copy lives here in a denser form
  than the HTML and is often the easiest place to read or diff actual page content.
- `_next/static/chunks/` — content-hashed JS bundles (framework, app, per-page). `app/<route>/page-*.js` maps to each route.
- `_next/static/css/*.css` — single compiled Tailwind stylesheet.
- `_next/static/media/*.woff2` — self-hosted fonts (display / body / mono families).
- `_next/static/<buildId>/_buildManifest.js`, `_ssgManifest.js` — Next.js client manifests.
- `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, `og.png` — SEO / social assets. `sitemap.xml` enumerates the
  canonical route set and is regenerated per build (carries a `lastmod` timestamp).

No deploy config is checked in (no `netlify.toml`, `vercel.json`, `CNAME`, `_redirects`,
`.nojekyll`). Any host config lives in the source repo or the hosting dashboard.

## Previewing locally

No build step exists here — it is already built. Serve it as static files with clean-URL support:

```bash
npx serve .          # or:  npx http-server .  /  python3 -m http.server
```

Because routes are `folder/index.html`, a server that resolves directory indexes will route
correctly. Opening `index.html` from `file://` will break asset and font paths (they are
site-absolute, e.g. `/_next/...`); always serve over HTTP.

There is no test, lint, or typecheck command in this directory — those belong to the source repo.

## Content conventions (carried from source, visible in the markup)

These are baked into the exported HTML/RSC and should be preserved if you ever hand-edit, and
respected when writing source that regenerates this site:

- **Provenance legend** (footer, applied to every metric on the site): `●` measured (reproduced
  on our hardware), `○` target (engineering goal), `◆` reported (cited research figure). When a
  measured number conflicts with a reported one, the measured number wins everywhere else. Do not
  present targets or reported figures as present-tense product facts.
- **Brand / product accent tokens**: WDBX `#00D4FF`, ABI `#7C3AED`, Abbey `#10B981`. Tailwind
  utility names follow suit (`text-wdbx`, `text-abi`, `text-abbey`, plus surface tokens
  `bg-ink`, `bg-panel`, `border-line`, `surface`, `accent-edge`).
- **Entity facts** (JSON-LD in the root layout + footer): Machine Learning Advanced Innovations,
  Inc. (MLAI), Delaware C-Corp, Orlando FL; founder Donald Filimon (list only Donald for
  leadership/team). External links: `github.com/donaldfilimon/abi` (Apache-2.0),
  `donaldfilimon.github.io/abi` (docs), `donaldfilimon.com` (founder).
- **Contact addresses** present in `contact/`: `enterprise@mlai.dev`, `invest@mlai.dev`,
  `careers@mlai.dev`.

## The three products described by the site

Useful orientation when reading or editing copy (each has its own route):

- **WDBX** (`/wdbx`) — Zig-built vector database: HNSW indexing, MVCC transactions, hash-chained
  WAL, Metal/CUDA/Vulkan backends.
- **ABI Framework** (`/abi`) — ML + GPU acceleration framework in Zig 0.17-dev + Metal: tensor
  ops, NN layers, zero-copy unified-memory pipelines.
- **Abbey** (`/abbey`) — self-learning, on-device AI assistant with persistent vector-backed
  memory.

Public copy must stay within the external-claim boundaries in the global instructions: frame
unproven performance/scale/security/traction claims as targets or design intent, grounded in
verifiable artifacts, not as production guarantees.

## Design system

See `DESIGN.md` for the component specs, states, and responsive behavior (the source-repo design
handoff). It catalogs the source components (`Nav`, `Section`, `StatBlock`, `FAQList`, etc.) and
the cross-cutting contracts — the accent contract (one of `wdbx | abi | abbey` per page, driven
through `--accent`), the provenance legend, the `md` (768px) desktop/mobile fork, and the
`prefers-reduced-motion` rule. Those components live in source, not in this export, but the doc is
the decoder ring for the rendered markup here.
